content.text:
Close works and selection persists (6 zones still legal) but sheet hidden. Nice.

Now test result screen via automation. Need be at 390 start; better use 1050 for performance. We can run async eval loop clicking end if enabled. But app's AI turn is async and end button disabled during AI; our loop must wait. Use:
```
async () => {
 const sleep=ms=>new Promise(r=>setTimeout(r,ms));
 let count=0;
 for (let i=0;i<30 && document.querySelector('#resultScreen').hidden;i++){
   const end=document.querySelector("button[data-act='end']");
   if(end && !end.disabled){ end.click(); count++; }
   await sleep(1200);
 }
 return {count, result:!document.querySelector('#resultScreen').hidden, lp:...}
}
```
This will run up to 36s. But each AI turn may take several seconds; if we poll every 1.2s and click end whenever enabled, fine. However if we click end during player's turn while `busy` false; good. It will keep ending turns. Need shell timeout > 60s. Let's try at 1050. But after reload/start. Then run loop. It might finish or not. We'll see.

