Now let's consider one more layout: 1181 exactly, rail appears, cardDetail hides. At 1181, stage columns 1fr 282; board slot width min(7vw=82.7, 8.6vh) at 900 = 77.4; board width 6*77.4+5*6.5=497; stage width 1181-24=1157 -282 -14=861; board fits. Good.

At 1181x600 (short desktop), slot width min(82.7,51.6)=51.6; board ~340; stage height 600-12-46-? handbar 170 = ~372, board 4*70=280, fits. Good.

Now maybe 1024x768 and 768x1024 (iPad portrait). 768x1024 falls 761-1180 side panel; board width 6*53.7+5*4.2=343, side panel 180 at right x 580, board right 555; gap 25. Good. Portrait tablet has lots of vertical space. Fine.

Phone landscape at 844x390 we saw. The side details sits right, board centered left, plate bottom right. Good.

Now one issue: the CSS `@media (orientation: landscape) and (max-height: 540px)` sets `.stage { position: relative; }` and `.duelist` absolute. But the `.card-detail` is position fixed; its top 124; good. At 844x390, card detail height 108, ends 230; player plate 245. fine. At 740x360 (width <=760, so cardDetail full width top 92; height maybe 110 ends 202; board? stage between 32 and 258, board 4*? slot-w clamp(40,5.4vh=19.4,52)=40 -> 4*54+10=228; centered board top 33, bottom 261. Detail top 92-202 covers AI rows and center. Could be an issue on small landscape width 740. But the full-width detail would cover a large part of the board. However 740x360 landscape is a phone; with side panel disabled because width <=760. Maybe use side panel for landscape regardless of width? At 740, board centered width 263, board right 501; side panel width 180 right 8 -> left 552, gap. It would fit! So cardDetail side panel could apply for any landscape orientation, even width <=760, except when width < 600 maybe. But CSS media can target `(orientation: landscape) and (max-height: 540px)` to force side panel. At 740x360, yes side panel at right. At 600x360? Board width 263, center 300, right 431; panel left 412 -> overlaps slightly 19px. At 568x320, board right 415, panel left 380, overlap 35. Could set panel width 160 for small landscape, but still. Hmm.

Maybe keep it simple: for `(orientation: landscape) and (max-height: 540px)` set card detail side width 160, right 6, top 40? Actually at 844 width panel at right fine. At 600, left 434, board right 431, just fit. At 568, left 402, board right 415, overlaps 13. Could hide card detail at max-width 600 landscape. Users on 568 landscape can tap card and see no details; but game still playable. Or use the top sheet? Hmm.

This is edge-case; standard phones at 844x390, 812x375, 667x375, 736x414. For 667x375: width <=760 -> full-width top sheet currently, would cover a lot. We should target landscape side panel for all landscape phones. At 667, board right 464; panel width 170 left 489, gap 25. Good. At 568, board right? slot 40 (min) => 6*40+5*4=260; center 284 -> right 414; panel width 160 left 402 overlap. Could set panel width 140 at max-width 640; left 422, gap 8. Text becomes narrow but okay. At 480x320 landscape, board 260 centered right 370; panel 130 left 344 overlap. But 480x320 is ancient.

Given support for modern phones, set landscape side panel `width: clamp(150px, 22vw, 200px)` and for max-width 760 landscape. At 667: 22vw=147 -> 150, left 511, board right 464, gap 47. At 568: 150, left 412, board right 414, overlap 2; borderline. Could set width 140 at <=600. Fine.

But another concern: in landscape max-height 540, the cardDetail top 116+6=122, height maybe 108, fits. For 667x375, handbar 115, topbar 30; same. Good.

Let's add:
```
@media (orientation: landscape) and (max-height: 540px) {
