But top 44? Enemy plate is top-left, no conflict; topbar 30. Set top: 40px maybe, so panel appears at top right; in 844 screenshot, currently panel at 122 (below board top) causing it to sit lower. If top 40, panel from 40-148 at right, board row right 553, no overlap. Better. In 844, the top right is empty; shows panel at top. But topbar is 30 high, so top 40. Great. At 667x375, panel top 40-148, right side, board right 464, panel left 509 -> no overlap. Fine.

This is extra polish. Do we need? It's likely nice. Let's implement landscape overrides after the card-detail media queries so they take precedence:
```
@media (orientation: landscape) and (max-height: 540px) {
  .card-detail { left:auto; right:max(8px,...); top: calc(max(2px,safe-top)+38px); width: clamp(150px,20vw,200px); }
